WEBVTT

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.250
"Xianyang"

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:10.340
<i>What</i>?!

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:13.880
The great Lord Biao--slain?

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:18.100
Lord Biao...

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:22.310
He died at the hand of the
enemy general, Pang Nuan.

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:27.610
Pang Nuan...

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:30.070
So they <i>did </i>bring him along.

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:33.400
And Lord Biao's army? Is it... wiped out?

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:38.070
No: some 2,000 escaped
and are en route to Xianyang.

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:39.950
Two thousand?

00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:41.490
Xin...

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:42.370
Report!

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:44.250
Oh, <i>now </i>what?

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:48.750
Riots have broken out in
some areas of Xianyang!

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:50.550
Riots?!

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:54.670
Sir! The enemy is so close
on the southern road

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:56.760
that the word is getting out:

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:59.350
both that General Biao has been slain

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:03.060
and that the opposing
general is Pang Nuan.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:06.980
There are rumors that
Xianyang has all but fallen,

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:11.020
and citizens are clashing with
the army as they try to leave.

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:12.230
Open up!

00:01:12.230 --> 00:01:13.820
Let us out!

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:16.400
Back off! We're blockading this gate!

00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:21.030
Report! Fires have broken
out throughout the city,

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:25.500
with citizens gathering at
the open northern gate!

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:27.830
We can't be infighting--not now!

00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:29.380
What on earth is going on?

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:32.250
Just how fiercely are these fires burning?

00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:35.010
Here we go.

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:39.720
Is there no word from Li Si?

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:47.480
Lord Changwen. A word?

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:49.190
Ah, Si Shi.

00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:51.520
Where have you been?

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:54.730
I've been keeping an eye
on Lü Buwei all this time.

00:01:54.730 --> 00:01:56.700
Lü Buwei?

00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:00.320
Li Si had been in hiding.
Now he's made a move.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:04.240
He's brought the Vermilion Slayers
into the Royal Court.

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:06.160
The Vermilion Slayers?

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:09.330
Does he mean to have
them fight for us, too?

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:10.960
Don't be absurd.

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:14.840
An assassin's job is only to assassinate.

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:17.590
And their target, most likely...

00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:19.220
...is our King.

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:23.390
Wh-What are you telling me--
and <i>now</i>, of all times!

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:25.600
This is when you need to hear it.

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:29.190
Do you think Lü Buwei is the kind of man

00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:32.440
who'd fight Li Mu and
Pang Nuan to the very end?

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:38.610
If we lose this battle,
he loses everything.

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:44.490
But right now, he has a way
to minimize his losses.

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:45.490
What?

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:49.830
Broker peace with Li Mu and,
having so distinguished himself,

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:51.710
arrange to keep his position--

00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:54.090
with his superb bargaining skills.

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:58.170
Broker peace? He can't possibly
reach a truce now--

00:02:58.170 --> 00:02:59.720
He can.

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:04.850
If the coalition army wants
Qin destroyed, so be it.

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:06.770
In other words...

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:12.150
If he offers up our King's head and
Xianyang in a bloodless surrender,

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:15.820
he stands to benefit from his generosity.

00:03:21.110 --> 00:03:22.450
I remember...

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:28.620
But this castle lacks the capacity
to stop Li Mu's army.

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:32.170
Is <i>that </i>what he meant?

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:37.550
It-It's hopeless. How can we fight
an enemy army like this?

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:42.340
Just see to it that His Highness
is never left alone.

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:46.260
I'll deal with the Vermilion Slayers;
you handle Li Mu's--

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:52.140
The King is gone!

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:53.690
<i>What</i>?!

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:26.740
"Zheng's Decision"

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:31.200
Si Shi is frantic, having realized
that Li Si is on the move.

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:35.210
If the King's faction has picked
up on Chancellor Lü's plans,

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:37.330
they might make the first move.

00:05:37.330 --> 00:05:41.590
Shall we increase Chancellor Lü's
security, just in case?

00:05:41.590 --> 00:05:44.920
I've yet to hear anything
from the chancellor.

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:47.840
We need do nothing just yet.

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:50.260
I'll speak with Li Si directly and--

00:05:51.390 --> 00:05:52.810
Y-Your Highness?!

00:05:58.100 --> 00:06:01.940
The King's entirely alone--
and what's more,

00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:03.900
he's armed.

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:07.360
He must know something's going on.

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:09.780
How may I be of service?

00:06:11.740 --> 00:06:13.990
Our nation is in crisis.

00:06:13.990 --> 00:06:15.870
I seek your opinion as our high commander,

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:18.370
now distanced from Lü's Four Pillars.

00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:22.710
Be brief, if possible.

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:27.760
I agree that Xianyang cannot
properly defend itself.

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:32.100
That is clear, given that it is now
trying to destroy itself from within.

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:38.390
And with Lord Biao's death,
we have no options left on the outside.

00:06:38.390 --> 00:06:40.310
No...

00:06:40.310 --> 00:06:42.810
I believe one option still remains.

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:46.070
Which is?

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:48.360
Zui.

00:06:52.570 --> 00:06:54.530
Huang Li, Ke Liang.

00:06:54.530 --> 00:06:58.120
Go on ahead and stall our guests.

00:06:58.120 --> 00:06:59.500
Meanwhile...

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:01.170
I'll stay here and talk a while.

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:22.190
Your Highness!

00:07:24.150 --> 00:07:28.570
I had no time to see you.
I must have worried you, Xiang.

00:07:28.570 --> 00:07:30.240
No... no!

00:07:33.990 --> 00:07:36.490
Are you feeling well?

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:41.250
Yes. It's been so hard
all this time, but now...

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:47.920
You've... lost a little weight,
Your Highness.

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:49.010
Have I?

00:07:52.590 --> 00:07:56.180
What... what will become of us all?

00:07:56.180 --> 00:07:58.220
Qin,

00:07:58.220 --> 00:07:59.770
Your Highness,

00:07:59.770 --> 00:08:01.350
the child in my belly...

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:09.070
I can't go into details for lack of time,
but the situation is tense.

00:08:09.070 --> 00:08:11.240
Xianyang itself is in danger.

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:12.450
Th-Then--

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:15.160
But I shall fight, too,
and not give up hope.

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:18.950
Your Highness, too?

00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:24.580
If I do join the fight,
I can't return until it's over--

00:08:24.580 --> 00:08:28.210
or rather, until the battle is won.

00:08:28.210 --> 00:08:32.010
I've come to see you while I still can.

00:08:32.010 --> 00:08:33.010
Eh?

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:36.180
I won't see him until he wins?

00:08:36.180 --> 00:08:38.810
And... if he doesn't?

00:08:38.810 --> 00:08:40.390
Is this our last--

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:43.940
No... no, it can't be!

00:08:43.940 --> 00:08:46.310
Your Highness, it's time.

00:08:46.310 --> 00:08:47.520
Coming.

00:08:48.650 --> 00:08:50.320
Y-Your Highness!

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:54.740
Um, actually, I think my belly's
grown bigger lately!

00:08:55.820 --> 00:08:58.620
What am I saying?

00:08:58.620 --> 00:09:00.620
So please--

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:04.370
Don't worry, Xiang.
I <i>will </i>come back to you.

00:09:05.370 --> 00:09:09.750
He's lying. I can hear it
in His Highness's voice.

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:13.300
Please--don't go.

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:17.050
If we're all going to die anyway,
let me die with you.

00:09:17.050 --> 00:09:19.550
I want to be with you!

00:09:19.550 --> 00:09:21.100
Your Highness!

00:09:25.310 --> 00:09:27.480
May fortune be yours.

00:09:30.820 --> 00:09:33.110
Yes. I'll be back.

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:54.510
Your Highness... Your Highness!

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:03.680
Our only hope in battle

00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:06.180
is at the end of the southern road:

00:10:06.180 --> 00:10:10.190
Zui, standing at the very
throat of Xianyang.

00:10:10.190 --> 00:10:13.270
With the Wei River between
Zui and Xianyang,

00:10:13.270 --> 00:10:17.070
the foe cannot move onward
without capturing Zui.

00:10:17.070 --> 00:10:18.820
Exactly right.

00:10:18.820 --> 00:10:24.580
But the majority of Zui's army has
been sent to Hangu Pass as well.

00:10:24.580 --> 00:10:26.660
There are civilians.

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:29.330
I believe Zui is quite populous.

00:10:29.330 --> 00:10:32.540
I had considered Zui myself.

00:10:32.540 --> 00:10:36.210
Fighting Li Mu with
an army of civilians...

00:10:36.210 --> 00:10:40.300
We would need a commander
on a par with the great generals

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:43.260
to spark a fire in their hearts.

00:10:43.260 --> 00:10:45.470
But with Lord Biao dead,

00:10:45.470 --> 00:10:48.480
we no longer have a commander
capable of such a feat.

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:51.690
Even I am not up to the task.

00:10:51.690 --> 00:10:55.940
No--one such person yet remains,

00:10:55.940 --> 00:10:57.320
though not a commander.

00:10:59.610 --> 00:11:02.740
You don't mean... Your Highness?

00:11:02.740 --> 00:11:03.740
I do.

00:11:04.910 --> 00:11:06.160
I shall go.

00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:09.710
Are your preparations complete?

00:11:15.880 --> 00:11:17.590
Qin's not done for just yet!

00:11:19.090 --> 00:11:20.340
Move out!

00:11:26.010 --> 00:11:27.470
"Qin"

00:11:27.470 --> 00:11:31.350
The king himself has set out
from Xianyang?!

00:11:31.350 --> 00:11:33.310
Th-The king...

00:11:33.310 --> 00:11:34.980
...has set out?

00:11:34.980 --> 00:11:41.070
His Highness has sallied forth to do
battle in Zui, the throat of Xianyang.

00:11:41.070 --> 00:11:46.370
Meanwhile, we are to prepare
for anything that might happen.

00:11:46.370 --> 00:11:47.790
Inconceivable!

00:11:47.790 --> 00:11:50.000
The King himself, on the battlefield?

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:54.170
And Lord Changwen's gone with him!
Talk about selfish!

00:11:54.170 --> 00:11:58.840
His Highness has left because
we can do no fighting here!

00:11:58.840 --> 00:12:03.510
And <i>that </i>is all because of your faction!

00:12:03.510 --> 00:12:06.850
--Wha--
--Just what do you mean by that, Si Shi?!

00:12:06.850 --> 00:12:09.770
You don't know? Then ask your master!

00:12:09.770 --> 00:12:11.060
What?!

00:12:11.060 --> 00:12:14.020
This act, this... reckless behavior.

00:12:14.020 --> 00:12:18.820
It's too drastic to have been
decided by just one person.

00:12:18.820 --> 00:12:20.320
Lord Changping.

00:12:20.320 --> 00:12:25.820
I heard you met with the King yesterday.

00:12:25.820 --> 00:12:31.250
You didn't happen to offer His Highness
any <i>advice</i>, now, did you--

00:12:31.250 --> 00:12:34.670
Lord Changping, one of my Four Pillars?

00:12:41.550 --> 00:12:44.300
Consider the situation, Chancellor.

00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:49.390
I am also high commander of the Qin army.

00:12:49.390 --> 00:12:51.930
Right now, everything else

00:12:51.930 --> 00:12:53.980
is of no consequence.

00:12:57.110 --> 00:13:03.070
Oho. These words of yours are not
to be taken lightly, Lord Changping.

00:13:05.610 --> 00:13:09.620
Although I suppose there's nothing
to be done about his escape.

00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:13.330
Perhaps <i>I </i>shall sit on the
now-vacant Jeweled Throne

00:13:13.330 --> 00:13:17.710
and contemplate what is to come.

00:13:17.710 --> 00:13:19.790
You'll <i>what</i>?!

00:13:19.790 --> 00:13:23.050
--Wait just a--
--Have you lost your mind, Lü Buwei?

00:13:26.180 --> 00:13:28.850
Why, the Jeweled Throne

00:13:28.850 --> 00:13:33.220
belongs to the royal
family now and forever,

00:13:33.220 --> 00:13:35.440
you absolute scoundrel.

00:13:36.850 --> 00:13:38.520
Cheng Jiao?

00:13:39.610 --> 00:13:40.570
Move.

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:03.460
B-But Cheng Jiao, my lord, that's--

00:14:05.170 --> 00:14:09.300
Don't get so flustered, Si Shi.
I spoke with him before he left.

00:14:11.510 --> 00:14:15.310
With His Highness--before he left?

00:14:15.310 --> 00:14:16.310
That's right.

00:14:20.110 --> 00:14:22.190
Meanwhile, on the southern road,

00:14:22.190 --> 00:14:25.690
we find the exhausted Xin and companions.

00:14:25.690 --> 00:14:28.450
The Li Mu Army had been in hot pursuit

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:31.570
of the Fei Xin Force and other
remnants of Lord Biao's army.

00:14:39.710 --> 00:14:41.920
Huh? Xianyang?

00:14:41.920 --> 00:14:43.380
No...

00:14:43.380 --> 00:14:48.010
That's Zui. The last castle
on the southern road.

00:14:48.010 --> 00:14:51.850
Once we pass this,
we'll be at Xianyang, Xin.

00:14:54.100 --> 00:14:56.350
The gates are open.

00:14:56.350 --> 00:14:58.270
For us?

00:14:58.270 --> 00:15:01.770
Let's stop a while and
find something to eat.

00:15:01.770 --> 00:15:03.650
Water, at the very least.

00:15:32.970 --> 00:15:34.970
Zh... Zheng?

00:15:37.890 --> 00:15:39.930
Xin.

00:15:39.930 --> 00:15:44.560
Huh? But what... what're you doin' here?

00:15:44.560 --> 00:15:48.490
I've come to fight beside you, of course.

00:15:51.910 --> 00:15:53.320
To fight?

00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:56.330
Zheng...

00:15:56.330 --> 00:15:59.700
They killed General Biao.

00:16:02.750 --> 00:16:05.790
The rest of us are in tatters.

00:16:05.790 --> 00:16:11.090
The enemy--Li Mu and
Pang Nuan are right behind us.

00:16:12.010 --> 00:16:15.010
Our commanders, Meng Wu
and Huan Yi and the rest,

00:16:15.010 --> 00:16:17.970
they're all at Hangu Pass, and...

00:16:22.270 --> 00:16:23.270
Yeah.

00:16:24.690 --> 00:16:29.320
We... we can still fight.

00:16:31.280 --> 00:16:35.200
We can still...

00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:38.410
We'll fend them off right here, Xin.

00:16:39.790 --> 00:16:40.790
Zheng!

00:16:43.420 --> 00:16:47.590
Can I just... lean on you for a sec?

00:16:47.590 --> 00:16:49.880
Sorry.

00:16:49.880 --> 00:16:51.920
Not at all.

00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:54.800
I've leaned on <i>you </i>time and time again.

00:16:58.810 --> 00:17:02.600
This... isn't Zui's official army, is it.

00:17:02.600 --> 00:17:03.770
No.

00:17:03.770 --> 00:17:07.480
There's something strangely...
<i>majestic </i>about them.

00:17:07.480 --> 00:17:10.320
Especially the guy Xin's chatting with.

00:17:10.320 --> 00:17:16.030
Yeah--like he's got this completely
different feel about him.

00:17:16.030 --> 00:17:19.160
Who the heck <i>is </i>that guy, anyway?

00:17:23.290 --> 00:17:24.620
What?!

00:17:24.620 --> 00:17:27.710
That was the King of Qin?!

00:17:27.710 --> 00:17:29.000
Yep.

00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:30.920
Th-The king...

00:17:30.920 --> 00:17:35.050
Brigade Commander Bi said so, too!

00:17:35.050 --> 00:17:37.050
Now hang on just one second!

00:17:37.050 --> 00:17:39.430
<i>This </i>one was talking
like they were equals!

00:17:39.430 --> 00:17:40.930
Like <i>that </i>would happen!

00:17:40.930 --> 00:17:41.720
Oh!

00:17:41.720 --> 00:17:43.600
You can't fool <i>us</i>, dammit!

00:17:43.600 --> 00:17:46.900
Look, it's like I've been tellin' you:

00:17:46.900 --> 00:17:51.270
We fought together when his
little brother started an uprising.

00:17:51.270 --> 00:17:53.900
Who's gonna believe a story like <i>that</i>?

00:17:53.900 --> 00:17:56.990
It's got to be some delusion or--

00:17:56.990 --> 00:18:02.660
Now that you mention it, wasn't that
guy the spitting image of Piao?

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:04.540
Oh! You're right!

00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:08.080
He really is Qin's... king.

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:09.080
Yep.

00:18:09.080 --> 00:18:11.800
Oh, so that's our king.

00:18:11.800 --> 00:18:15.010
I-I guess he really <i>does </i>exist.

00:18:15.010 --> 00:18:16.720
'Course he does.

00:18:16.720 --> 00:18:21.300
Wow! You could go your whole life and
not see the king with your own eyes!

00:18:21.300 --> 00:18:23.010
I'm gonna brag about this back home!

00:18:23.010 --> 00:18:27.100
But, I mean... the king sure is amazing.

00:18:27.100 --> 00:18:31.770
Yeah--it's like he was
practically glowing.

00:18:31.770 --> 00:18:33.900
Dammit. This is the worst.

00:18:33.900 --> 00:18:38.150
I just had to be all pathetic
with him. Me, of all people.

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:42.200
Well, whatever!

00:18:42.200 --> 00:18:43.790
Where are you going, Xin?

00:18:43.790 --> 00:18:45.290
Over by Zheng.

00:18:45.290 --> 00:18:46.500
Eh?

00:18:46.500 --> 00:18:47.540
Hey!

00:18:47.540 --> 00:18:50.540
Don't call the king by his first name!

00:18:50.540 --> 00:18:55.760
Hey... maybe Xin really <i>is</i>
this super-incredible guy.

00:18:55.760 --> 00:18:58.170
I-I'm not so sure myself anymore.

00:18:58.170 --> 00:19:00.470
No, he's totally just some idiot.

00:19:00.470 --> 00:19:02.680
At least Xin's feeling better.

00:19:08.350 --> 00:19:09.890
Hey.

00:19:09.890 --> 00:19:11.190
Done crying?

00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:15.150
Shut up! Don't laugh, damn you!

00:19:15.150 --> 00:19:19.450
What's a King like you doin' leavin'
Xianyang in the first place?

00:19:19.450 --> 00:19:24.030
From what I hear, Lü Buwei and Lord
Changping and all them ain't left!

00:19:24.030 --> 00:19:25.040
Well--

00:19:26.450 --> 00:19:28.330
Dammit! It's no good!

00:19:28.330 --> 00:19:30.830
It's just hopeless, Zheng!

00:19:30.830 --> 00:19:31.670
Diao!

00:19:31.670 --> 00:19:35.210
Oh, Xin! You're done crying? Good.

00:19:35.210 --> 00:19:36.340
Shut <i>up</i>!

00:19:38.130 --> 00:19:42.470
Zui's construction has
its good and bad points.

00:19:42.470 --> 00:19:45.390
A plus: its gates are strong.

00:19:45.390 --> 00:19:48.560
They won't be broken down that easily.

00:19:48.560 --> 00:19:52.350
A minus: its walls are hardly tall enough.

00:19:52.350 --> 00:19:55.690
A long ladder would be all it takes.

00:19:55.690 --> 00:19:58.780
A free-for-all on the castle walls, eh?

00:19:58.780 --> 00:20:02.240
But that's what castle
defense is all about.

00:20:02.240 --> 00:20:05.200
I wouldn't particularly call it hopeless.

00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:07.950
The castle's not the problem here.

00:20:07.950 --> 00:20:11.790
Zui doesn't have enough
troops to call an army.

00:20:11.790 --> 00:20:14.040
Their main forces,
along with their official army,

00:20:14.040 --> 00:20:16.630
are almost all at Hangu Pass.

00:20:16.630 --> 00:20:18.460
What's left?

00:20:18.460 --> 00:20:19.760
A thousand.

00:20:19.760 --> 00:20:23.640
A <i>thousand</i>?! Li Mu's got over 30,000!

00:20:23.640 --> 00:20:27.180
We've only got about
2,000 troops ourselves...

00:20:27.180 --> 00:20:28.310
I know!

00:20:28.310 --> 00:20:33.270
Zheng, how many troops did
you bring outta Xianyang?

00:20:33.270 --> 00:20:34.900
Just under 2,000.

00:20:34.900 --> 00:20:37.860
That's <i>it</i>?! That's nothin'!

00:20:37.860 --> 00:20:40.610
Why did you leave Xianyang with <i>that</i>?

00:20:40.610 --> 00:20:41.530
Various reasons.

00:20:41.530 --> 00:20:44.360
So <i>tell </i>me them!

00:20:44.360 --> 00:20:47.830
Look, we've got under
5,000 versus over 30,000--

00:20:47.830 --> 00:20:50.910
with the enemy scramblin'
up over these walls, too!

00:20:50.910 --> 00:20:53.500
And this is the Li Mu Army
we're up against.

00:20:53.500 --> 00:20:56.580
I gotta be honest: This ain't a battle.

00:20:58.250 --> 00:21:00.710
No; there's still hope.

00:21:05.140 --> 00:21:06.640
Lord Changwen!

00:21:06.640 --> 00:21:08.600
My lord!

00:21:08.600 --> 00:21:11.220
Reporting, Sire.

00:21:11.220 --> 00:21:14.020
Zui is home to about 30,000.

00:21:14.020 --> 00:21:18.060
But there are few men, most having
been dispatched to Hangu Pass;

00:21:18.060 --> 00:21:22.190
20,000 of that number are women,
children, and the elderly.

00:21:22.190 --> 00:21:23.190
Huh?

00:21:25.240 --> 00:21:26.990
Thirty thousand?

00:21:26.990 --> 00:21:29.700
Good. They lost fewer than I'd expected.

00:21:29.700 --> 00:21:30.990
Eh?

00:21:30.990 --> 00:21:34.080
That gives us 35,000 altogether.

00:21:36.250 --> 00:21:40.800
You're not seriously gonna
rely on <i>civilians </i>in this fight!

00:21:40.800 --> 00:21:42.550
Y-Your Highness!

00:21:42.550 --> 00:21:44.800
War is serious business, Zheng!

00:21:44.800 --> 00:21:47.390
And half of 'em are women and children?

00:21:47.390 --> 00:21:48.800
Are you shittin' me?!

00:21:48.800 --> 00:21:55.980
Quiet, Xin. We have no choice
but to fight with what we have.

00:21:55.980 --> 00:21:57.440
With what we have?

00:21:57.440 --> 00:22:01.110
You <i>know </i>that women and kids don't count!

00:22:01.110 --> 00:22:04.610
Zheng... I think I see
what you're going for.

00:22:04.610 --> 00:22:07.360
Logistical support is key
in castle defense--

00:22:07.360 --> 00:22:11.160
it's the easiest battle for
amateurs to be a part of.

00:22:11.160 --> 00:22:14.200
But before we talk about tactics,

00:22:14.200 --> 00:22:18.880
everyone <i>must </i>have that fighting
spirit--or we won't have a battle at all.

00:22:18.880 --> 00:22:21.460
We need everyone to be a soldier.

00:22:21.460 --> 00:22:23.760
When I made my rounds earlier, I learned

00:22:23.760 --> 00:22:27.800
that Zui here is hopeless,
as far as that goes.

00:22:27.800 --> 00:22:29.800
What do you mean, Diao?

00:22:29.800 --> 00:22:35.980
Zui had been planning to open its gates
to Li Mu and surrender all along.

00:22:35.980 --> 00:22:40.770
Those 30,000 are in there
because they'd given up.

00:22:40.770 --> 00:22:42.770
Wh-<i>What</i>?!

00:22:45.990 --> 00:22:46.860
Diao.

00:22:46.860 --> 00:22:49.450
I know it's verging on unwise.

00:22:49.450 --> 00:22:51.990
But if we have even the slightest chance,

00:22:51.990 --> 00:22:54.950
all we can do now is jump at it.

00:22:54.950 --> 00:22:58.540
If you're saying that
only soldiers may fight,

00:22:58.540 --> 00:23:01.290
my role is to make soldiers
of everyone here.

00:23:03.750 --> 00:23:07.170
We still have a little time
before Li Mu's army arrives.

00:23:07.170 --> 00:23:10.140
Come, Xin--and bring your troops.

00:23:13.260 --> 00:23:17.020
There's something I want everyone to hear.

00:24:54.320 --> 00:24:58.660
Next on <i>Kingdom</i>: "Zheng Speaks."
